==============================================================================
ADJUDICATION ADDENDUM (same session, split-invariance test)
==============================================================================
A_c AS PRE-REGISTERED IS VOID. Recomputing the chord-intersection A_c with
the window split at 0.35/0.50/0.65 of the overlap ln-span moves A_c by
15-42% per run, tracking the split (monotone in nine of ten runs) -- the two-chord
intersection follows the split point when sigma(A) curves smoothly instead
of breaking sharply. The A_c point values above, and the ln A_c vs ln nu
slope (+0.010), are estimator geometry, not physics. Retracted as
measurements; retained as the record of a pre-registered definition failing
its invariance test.

WHAT SURVIVES, AND WHY IT IS ESTIMATOR-INDEPENDENT:
1. THE FLAT EXPONENT CURVE. sigma_deep(nu) = -1.12..-1.29 at every nu in
   {1e-5..1e-3}, every point under the 0.15 cross-grid bar, anchors
   replicated 4/4 against the certified M4 values at different snapshot
   cadence. With the nu=0 matched anchor at +0.589, the inversion is a
   nu -> 0+ DISCONTINUITY of the deep-collapse exponent over the
   accessible range, not a gradual crossover in nu. (Consistent with the
   Corollary-0 reading: the cap exists for every nu > 0, is absent at 0.)
2. THE CROSSOVER BRACKET. Independently of any A_c estimator: at every nu,
   the lower half of the fixed overlap window reads inviscid-like
   (positive slope) and the upper half reads deeply depleted (~-1.2).
   That brackets the crossover inside the same fixed amplitude band at
   all five viscosities -- over two decades of nu it does NOT track the
   viscous scale. Where the crossover lives is set by something
   nu-independent; what that is remains open.
3. DENSITY FIX CONFIRMED: top windows now n=20-27 (was 11-14), CIs
   tighter, at 2x snapshot cadence.
